ent of solid tumors; and ZW1528, a bispecific molecule to treat chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. It has strategic partnerships and collaborations with Jazz Pharmaceuticals plc; Bristol- Myers Squibb company; Celgene Alpine Investment Co. LLC; GlaxoSmithKline Intellectual Property Development Limited; Daiichi Sankyo Co., Ltd.; Merck Sharp & Dohme Research GmbH; and Janssen Biotech, Inc. Zymeworks Inc. was incorporated in 2003 and is based in Middletown, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kenneth H. Galbraith C.A. | Chairman of the Board, CEO & President | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 279 people. Revenue per employee of $380K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 36%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $100K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Zymeworks Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.8B market cap on $106M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -36% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -56% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $35M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 26% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, 